:: Fishing Bait Widgets [widget]

<<widget "baitOverlay">>
	<<fishingBaitList>>
	<label class="fishing-select-bait-radio">
		<<checkbox "$fishing.autoRebait" false true autocheck>> Automatically re-bait
	</label>
	<br><br>

	<<if $fishingSelectedBait is "none" or _fishingHaveBait is true>>
		<<link "Change bait">>
			<<if $fishing.currentBait and $fishing.currentBait isnot $fishingSelectedBait>>
				<<run baitReturn($fishing.currentBait)>>
			<</if>>
			<<if $fishingSelectedBait is "none">>
				<<unset $fishing.currentBait>>
			<<else>>
				<<if $fishingSelectedBait isnot $fishing.currentBait>>
					<<run baitTake($fishingSelectedBait)>>
				<</if>>
				<<set $fishing.currentBait to $fishingSelectedBait>>
			<</if>>
			<<unset $fishingSelectedBait>>
			<<set _hasBait to $fishing.currentBait and setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait]>>
			<<set _newBaitTooltip to _hasBait ? "Bait: " + baitLabel($fishing.currentBait) : "No bait on your line (click to change)">>
			<<if elementExists("#bait-sidebar")>>
				<<replace "#bait-sidebar">>
					<<if _hasBait>>
						<<baiticon $fishing.currentBait>>
					<<else>>
						<<icon `"fish/hook.png"`>>
					<</if>>
				<</replace>>
				<<run jQuery("#bait-sidebar").attr("tooltip", "<span>" + _newBaitTooltip + "</span>").removeData("tooltip-settings")>>
			<</if>>
			<<if elementExists("#bait-mobile-sidebar")>>
				<<replace "#bait-mobile-sidebar">>
					<<if _hasBait>>
						<<baiticon $fishing.currentBait>>
					<<else>>
						<<icon `"fish/hook.png"`>>
					<</if>>
				<</replace>>
				<<run jQuery("#bait-mobile-sidebar").attr("tooltip", "<span>" + _newBaitTooltip + "</span>").removeData("tooltip-settings")>>
			<</if>>
			<<run closeOverlay()>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingBaitHelp">>
The goal of fishing is simple: reel the fish in before it escapes, gets too far away, or breaks your line!
<br><br>
Different fish behave in different ways. Fish of the same type often share the same habits, so learning how one fish reacts can help you with others like it. Pay attention to how they move, then choose whether to reel, hold, or give them some slack!
<br><br>
Your arms get tired while you reel a fish in or try to hold it in place. Failing either action tires you even more. The more tired your arms are, the harder it becomes to control the fish.
If your arms need a rest, you can give the fish some slack. This lets you recover, but also gives the fish a chance to move farther away. Use it when you think you have enough room to spare!
<br><br>
Fishing without bait will still work, but you will see fewer bites.
Worms are easy to buy from the bait shop. They work best for sardines and other small fish. Many kinds of food can also be used as bait and work well for common fish.
Small live fish are different. They attract larger fish, which are usually harder to catch. A small bass, carp, herring, or trout can therefore be more useful as bait than something to sell.
Bait fish and your can of worms must be kept in your pocket or bag before you can use them.
Worms, the Bone Rod, and the Bone Reel each make small fish more likely to appear. Their bonuses stack when used together.
<br><br>
Each one attracts different larger fish:<br>
<span class="blue">Small herring</span> works best for large sea fish.<br>
<span class="blue">Small carp</span> works best for large, slow fish found in lakes and on the moor.<br>
<span class="blue">Small trout</span> works best in cold water and rivers.<br>
<span class="blue">Small bass</span> works best for large predators, especially freshwater fish.
<br><br>
Your rod and reel affect different parts of fishing:
<br>
The <span class="blue">rod</span> reduces strain and helps tire the fish out.<br>
The <span class="blue">reel</span> affects how much distance you gain or lose while reeling and giving slack.
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingRebaitMid">>
	<<set _rebaitLeft to baitUsableStock($fishing.currentBait)>>
	<<if _rebaitLeft lte 0>>
		baiting your <span class="red">last</span> piece of <<print setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait].plural>> on the hook and casting back out.
	<<else>>
		re-baiting your line and casting back out. You have <<= _rebaitLeft>> <<print setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait].plural>> left<<if $fishing.currentBait is "bait_worm" and wormCanUsable()>> in the can<</if>>.
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingRebaitStart">>
	<<set _rebaitLeft to baitUsableStock($fishing.currentBait)>>
	<<if _rebaitLeft lte 0>>
		You bait your <span class="red">last</span> piece of <<print setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait].plural>> on the hook and cast back out.
	<<else>>
		You re-bait your line and cast back out. You have <<= _rebaitLeft>> <<print setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait].plural>> left<<if $fishing.currentBait is "bait_worm" and wormCanUsable()>> in the can<</if>>.
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingBaitList">>
	<<unset $fishingSelectedBait>>

	<label class="fishing-select-bait-radio">
		<<icon `"fish/hook.png"`>> None
		<<if !$fishing.currentBait>>
			<<radiobutton "$fishingSelectedBait" "none" checked>>
		<<else>>
			<<radiobutton "$fishingSelectedBait" "none">>
		<</if>>
		|
	</label>

	<<set _foodKeys to baitOrderedKeys()>>
	<<for _i to 0; _i lt _foodKeys.length; _i++>>
		<<set _food to _foodKeys[_i]>>
		<<if setup.foodstuff[_food].is_fishing_bait is true and baitStock(_food) gte 1>>
			<<if baitUsable(_food)>>
				<<set _fishingHaveBait to true>>
				<<if !$fishingSelectedBait and $fishing.currentBait is _food>>
					<<set $fishingSelectedBait to _food>>
				<</if>>
				<label class="fishing-select-bait-radio">
					<<baiticon _food>><<= baitLabel(_food)>>
					<<if _food is $fishingSelectedBait>>
						<<radiobutton "$fishingSelectedBait" _food checked>>
					<<else>>
						<<radiobutton "$fishingSelectedBait" _food>>
					<</if>>
					|
				</label>
			<<else>>
				/* Owned, but left at home. Shown so the reason is obvious rather than the bait simply missing. */
				<label class="fishing-select-bait-radio bait-unpacked">
					<<baiticon _food>><span class="grey"><<= baitLabel(_food)>> not in your pocket</span>
					|
				</label>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<</for>>
	<br><br>
<</widget>>

/* Bait worms coming out of the tin show the tin. */
<<widget "baiticon">>
	<<if _args[0] is "bait_worm" and wormCanOwned() and baitLooseStock("bait_worm") is 0>>
		<<icon `"fish/mod/wormcan.png"`>>
	<<else>>
		<<foodstufficon _args[0]>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "baitSidebar">>
	<<set $fishing.displayBaitNotification ??= true>>
	<<set _baitEditEnabled to canOpenBaitOverlay()>>
	<<if $fishing?.currentBait and setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait]>>
		<<set _baitTooltip to "Bait: " + baitLabel($fishing.currentBait)>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _baitTooltip to "No bait on your line (click to change)">>
	<</if>>
	<button type="button" id="bait-sidebar" @class="'bait-sidebar' + (_baitEditEnabled ? '' : ' bait-sidebar-disabled') + ($fishing.displayBaitNotification ? ' bait-sidebar-notify' : '')" tooltip="<span>_baitTooltip</span>" onclick="openBaitOverlay(); this.classList.remove('bait-sidebar-notify');">
		<<if $fishing?.currentBait and setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait]>>
			<<baiticon $fishing.currentBait>>
		<<else>>
			<<icon `"fish/hook.png"`>>
		<</if>>
	</button>
<</widget>>

<<widget "baitMobileDropdown">>
	<select id="fishing-bait-select" onchange="fishingChangeBaitFromDropdown(this.value)">
		<option value="none">None</option>
		<<set _foodKeys to baitOrderedKeys()>>
		<<for _i to 0; _i lt _foodKeys.length; _i++>>
			<<set _food to _foodKeys[_i]>>
			<<if setup.foodstuff[_food].is_fishing_bait is true and (baitUsable(_food) or $fishing.currentBait is _food)>>
				<option @value="_food"><<= baitLabel(_food)>></option>
			<</if>>
		<</for>>
	</select>
	<<timed 0s>><<run $("#fishing-bait-select").val($fishing.currentBait ? $fishing.currentBait : "none")>><</timed>>
	<br>
	<label class="fishing-select-bait-radio">
		<<checkbox "$fishing.autoRebait" false true autocheck>> Automatically re-bait
	</label>
<</widget>>

<<widget "baitMobileSidebar">>
	<<set _baitEditEnabled to canOpenBaitOverlay()>>
	<<if $fishing?.currentBait and setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait]>>
		<<set _baitTooltip to "Bait: " + baitLabel($fishing.currentBait)>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _baitTooltip to "No bait on your line (click to change)">>
	<</if>>
	<button type="button" id="bait-mobile-sidebar" @class="'bait-mobile-sidebar' + (_baitEditEnabled ? '' : ' bait-sidebar-disabled')" tooltip="<span>_baitTooltip</span>" onclick="openBaitOverlay()">
		<<if $fishing?.currentBait and setup.foodstuff[$fishing.currentBait]>>
			<<baiticon $fishing.currentBait>>
		<<else>>
			<<icon `"fish/hook.png"`>>
		<</if>>
	</button>
<</widget>>
